title BUHR-J7r2 — the manifest as the true index
prompt Continue the agent-doable journey; land BUHR-J7r2 as its own signed round; send often; stop at custody gates
think Rung one round-tripped the format tablecloth-v1 manifest through render and parse. The next crux the exploration named is the manifest as the true index — a parsed manifest verified against the live store it claims to describe.
think Exposed a small additive accessor on tablecloth.rye — address_hex (and address_hex_width) writes the content address a name pins, so the store's recorded address can be compared to a manifest's published one; made ManifestEntry pub so the reader can read published names and addresses.
think Wrote pond/apps/tablecloth_index.rye verify_against_store: for each published entry, fetch_artifact reassembles it (proving the beads by digest and the whole against the recorded address), the length must equal the published length, and address_hex must equal the published address.
obs The verification chains three proofs already earned: reassembly integrity (r1/beading), published length, and published address — so a missing name refuses UnknownArtifact, a wrong length LengthMismatch, a wrong address AddressMismatch. A person handed a manifest can audit the store artifact for artifact.
obs Built GREEN; rung one stays its own GREEN binary under the reader (additive). The address-mismatch case flips one hex nibble of the published address while leaving the store intact, so fetch and length still pass and only the address check bites — the refusals are independent.
obs TAME bans clean (parseInt ratchet holds at 8), width-check clean.
loom witness=buhr_tablecloth_index_witness verified=2 refusals=3 length=UnknownArtifact/LengthMismatch/AddressMismatch
file pond/apps/tablecloth_index.rye the index reader — verify_against_store proves a manifest is honest against the live store
file pond/apps/tablecloth.rye additive: pub address_hex + address_hex_width; ManifestEntry made pub for the reader
file tools/buhr_tablecloth_index_witness.rish the witness — verify 2, three refusals, r1 re-run
